<title>INDIA: Inflows/outflows of expatriate deposits - RBI.</title>
<headline>Inflows/outflows of expatriate deposits - RBI.</headline>
<text>
<p>Outstanding balances and Inflows(+)/Outflows(-)</p>
<p>		     under various NRI deposits @</p>
<p>							 (US $ Million)</p>
<p>			  Balances	     Inflows(+)/Outflows(-)</p>
<p>		  --------------------    -----------------------</p>
<p>    Item	End-	    End-	  1995-96     1994-95</p>
<p>		  March	   March</p>
<p>		  1996	    1995</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>FCNR(A)	 4,624	   7,051	 -2,427	-2,249</p>
<p>FCNR(B)	 5,723	   3,054	  2,669	 1,979</p>
<p>NR(E)RA	 4,004	   4,590	   -157	 1,000</p>
<p>NR(NR)D	 3,544	   2,479	  1,280	   682</p>
<p>FC(B&amp;O)D	    0		 0		0	  -558</p>
<p>Total	  17,895	  17,174	  1,365	   854*</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>@ All figures are inclusive of accrued interest.</p>
<p>* Net of FCON, it would be $847 million.</p>
<p>Note : The difference between the outstanding balances does not match with the inflow figures in case of rupee deposits because of the fluctuations in the exchange rate of the rupee during the year 1995/96 (April-March).</p>
<p>Source : Reserve Bank of india annual report for 1995/96 (July-June).</p>
